## Multiple ENV Variables
You can declare them in one `ENV` instruction (recommended) or separately:

```dockerfile
# Preferred - single instruction
ENV STUDENT_GOAL="Thinkbook" \
    STUDENT_NAME="John" \
    STUDY_HOURS="8" \
    COURSE="Docker"

# Also valid but less clean
ENV STUDENT_GOAL="Thinkbook"
ENV STUDENT_NAME="John"
ENV STUDY_HOURS="8"
```
The single instruction is preferred because each line in a Dockerfile creates a **new layer** — fewer instructions = smaller image.

